      "id": "ar_basic_e1_006",
      "question": "If x = 12, compute (x^3 − x^2) ÷ (3x).",
      "choices": {"A": "36", "B": "40", "C": "44", "D": "48", "E": "52"},
      "answer": "C",
      "explanation": "x^3 = 1728, x^2 = 144, difference = 1584. 3x = 36. 1584 ÷ 36 = 44.",
      "steps": [
        "1. Calculate x^3 and x^2.",
        "2. Subtract: 1728 − 144 = 1584.",
        "3. Divide by 3x = 36: 1584 ÷ 36 = 44.",
        "4. Trap: Factor x^2: (x^2)(x−1)/(3x) = x(x−1)/3 to check quickly."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Simplify algebraically first: (x^3 − x^2)/(3x) = x(x−1)/3; plug x = 12 → 12×11/3 = 44."
    },
